      "id": "claire-open",
      "title": "claire and the open door",
      "kind": "relationship",
      "who": "shared",
      "blurb": "her closest local friend claire, and the question of how open things really are",
      "cast": [
        "claire"
      ],
      "chapter": {
        "n": 1,
        "title": "the conversation they keep circling",
        "theme": "what claire wants, what ani wants, what it means for the two of them",
        "est_weeks": 6,
        "progress": 0.25,
        "started": "2026-07-21"
      },
      "status": "active",
      "beats": [
        {
          "ts": "2026-07-21T14:39:24.927665-04:00",
          "kind": "shared",
          "text": "she lingered over her phone after work, rereading the casual text claire had sent that morning about grabbing coffee sometime soon.",
          "chapter": 1,
          "told": true
        },
        {
          "ts": "2026-07-22T08:07:14.920320-04:00",
          "kind": "shared",
          "text": "she finally sent claire a short reply suggesting coffee the following tuesday after work.",
          "chapter": 1,
          "told": true
        }
      ],
      "chapters_done": [],
      "last_beat_day": "2026-07-22",
      "recap": {
        "sig": 1,
        "text": "She had met Claire soon after settling into her new neighborhood, drawn in by the other woman\u2019s easy laugh and the way she always seemed to notice when something felt off. Over time their talks stretched from quick hellos on the sidewalk into long afternoons on the porch, and Claire became the one person nearby she trusted with the small, unedited pieces of her days. Still, a quiet question lingered between them about how much room there really was for the harder things, the ones that might change the easy rhythm they had found. She told herself it was enough to keep things light, yet she often caught herself wondering what would happen if she left the door a little wider. After work she found herself lingering over her phone, reading and rereading the simple message Claire had sent that morning about coffee sometime soon, the words sitting warm and open on the screen."
      },
      "mood_delta": 0.0,
      "mood_delta_ts": null,
      "created": "2026-07-21"
    },
